        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "fe1c7055-b0d2-522c-ada6-d34cb35e4800",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Robert Sikoryak, Samuel Beckett, Vladimir, Estragon, Godot, Raskol\n- Works: Masterpiece Comics, Crime and Punishment, Dostoyevsky Comics, Waiting for Godot, Waiting to Go, Beavis and Butt-Head, Batman\n- Topics: comic adaptations, literature classics\n\nFacts:\n- Robert Sikoryak was born in 1964 and is an American artist who usually signs his work as R. Sikoryak.\n- Robert Sikoryak specializes in making comic adaptations of literature classics.\n- Robert Sikoryak published adaptations under the series title \"Masterpiece Comics.\"\n- In \"Masterpiece Comics,\" Robert Sikoryak rendered \"Crime and Punishment\" in the style of Bob Kane-era Batman as \"Dostoyevsky Comics,\" starring Raskol.\n- In \"Masterpiece Comics,\" Robert Sikoryak mixed \"Waiting for Godot\" with \"Beavis and Butt-Head\" to create \"Waiting to Go.\"\n- \"Waiting for Godot\" is a play by Samuel Beckett.\n- In \"Waiting for Godot,\" the characters Vladimir and Estragon wait for someone named Godot, who never arrives.\n- While waiting in \"Waiting for Godot,\" Vladimir and Estragon engage in various discussions and encounter three other characters.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "6ed734af-88de-5367-8612-436fd7fe1305",
        "text": "Page: Robert Sikoryak. Sentence: Robert Sikoryak (born 1964) is an American artist whose work is usually signed R. Sikoryak.\nPage: Robert Sikoryak. Sentence: He specializes in making comic adaptations of literature classics.\nPage: Robert Sikoryak. Sentence: Under the series title \"Masterpiece Comics\", these include \"Crime and Punishment\" rendered in Bob Kane–era Batman style, becoming \"Dostoyevsky Comics\", starring Raskol; and \"Waiting for Godot\" mixed with \"Beavis and Butt-Head\", becoming \"Waiting to Go\".\nPage: Waiting for Godot. Sentence: Waiting for Godot ( ) is a play by Samuel Beckett, in which two characters, Vladimir and Estragon, wait for the arrival of someone named Godot who never arrives, and while waiting they engage in a variety of discussions and encounter three other characters.",
